</div>
<p>Requesting these documents demonstrates your seriousness and forces the mover to operate within professional standards. If a company hesitates to provide basic licensing information, consider it a major warning sign.</div></div>
<h3>Red Flags to Watch For</h3>
<div style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.08); border-left: 4px solid #f59e0b; border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 18px 22px; margin: 24px 0;"><h4 style="color: #f59e0b; font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle" style="margin-right: 8px;"></i>Important Logistics Advisory</h4><div style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.92rem; margin: 0; line-height: 1.6;">Be vigilant for specific indicators of fraud or poor management. Common red flags include:</div></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>Refusal to Provide a Physical Address:</strong> Scammers often use only P.O. Boxes or temporary virtual offices.</li>
<li><strong>Pressure Tactics:</strong> Aggressive demands for immediate deposits without a proper inspection.</li>
<li><strong>Unrealistic Pricing:</strong> Quotes significantly lower than market average often signal hidden fees or lack of insurance.</li>
<li><strong>Vague Communication:</strong> Inability to answer specific questions about crew size, equipment, or timelines.</li>
</ul>
<p>By prioritizing the verification of a <strong>physical office address</strong> and demanding proper documentation, you protect your assets and your peace of mind. This due diligence ensures that your moving company is a legitimate, accountable partner in your relocation process, capable of handling your goods with the care and professionalism they deserve.</p></div>
